            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery fistula as a bypass of a left anterior descending coronary artery stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1813-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of coronary artery fistula originating from the proximal left anterior descending coronary artery anterior to a critical atheromatous stenosis, draining into the main trunk of the pulmonary artery and with a third branch draining into the coronary vessel itself, distal to the lesion. The diagnosis was made when we were performing a diagnostic coronary arteriography on a patient with unstable angina. The possible association of the fistula and coronary atherosclerosis is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
